    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br><br>On Friday, September 29, 2017 at 5:04:51 PM UTC-4, Haines, Nathaniel B. wrote:</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div>\r\n\r\n<div style=\"font-size:12pt;color:#000000;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif\" dir=\"ltr\">\r\n<p>Hi Joe, </p>\r\n<p><br>\r\n</p>\r\n<p>This is a complicated issue, so I understand your confusion! however, if you look at the model in more detail described on the page you are linking:</p>\r\n<p><br>\r\n</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<pre style=\"overflow:auto;font-size:15px;padding:10.5px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:11px;line-height:1.42857;word-break:break-all;word-wrap:break-word;color:rgb(51,51,51);border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);border-radius:4px\"><code style=\"font-size:inherit;padding:0px;color:inherit;background-color:transparent;border-radius:0px;white-space:pre-wrap\">data { \r\n  int&lt;lower=0&gt; N; \r\n  int&lt;lower=0, upper=1&gt; y[N]; \r\n} \r\nparameters { \r\n  real alpha; \r\n} \r\ntransformed parameters { \r\n  real&lt;lower=0, upper=1&gt; <span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,0)\">theta</span>; \r\n  <span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,0)\">theta</span> &lt;- inv_logit(alpha); \r\n} \r\nmodel { \r\n  for (n in 1:N) \r\n    y[n] ~ bernoulli(theta); \r\n  <span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,0)\">theta</span> ~ uniform(0, 1); \r\n} </code></pre>\r\n, you will see that theta is the transformed variable on the left side in the transformed parameters block, but also the same variable being distributed across in the model block. In this case, it is necessary to use the Jacobian adjustment. In hBayesDM, we\r\n do the following (from ra_noLA):\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p><br>\r\n</p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<pre style=\"overflow:auto;font-size:15px;padding:10.5px;margin-top:0px;margin-bottom:11px;line-height:1.42857;word-break:break-all;word-wrap:break-word;color:rgb(51,51,51);border:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);border-radius:4px\"><code style=\"font-size:inherit;padding:0px;color:inherit;background-color:transparent;border-radius:0px;white-space:pre-wrap\"><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif,Helvetica,EmojiFont,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,NotoColorEmoji,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Android Emoji&quot;,EmojiSymbols;font-size:16px\">transformed parameters {</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif,Helvetica,EmojiFont,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,NotoColorEmoji,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Android Emoji&quot;,EmojiSymbols;font-size:16px\">  vector&lt;lower=0,upper=2&gt;[N] <span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">rho</span>;</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif,Helvetica,EmojiFont,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,NotoColorEmoji,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Android Emoji&quot;,EmojiSymbols;font-size:16px\">  vector&lt;lower=0&gt;[N] <span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">tau</span>;</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif,Helvetica,EmojiFont,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,NotoColorEmoji,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Android Emoji&quot;,EmojiSymbols;font-size:16px\">     </div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif,Helvetica,EmojiFont,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,NotoColorEmoji,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Android Emoji&quot;,EmojiSymbols;font-size:16px\">  for (i in 1:N) {</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif,Helvetica,EmojiFont,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,NotoColorEmoji,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Android Emoji&quot;,EmojiSymbols;font-size:16px\">    <span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">rho</span>[i] = Phi_approx( mu_p[1] + sigma[1] * <span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,0)\">rho_p</span>[i] ) * 2;</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif,Helvetica,EmojiFont,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,NotoColorEmoji,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Android Emoji&quot;,EmojiSymbols;font-size:16px\">  }</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif,Helvetica,EmojiFont,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,NotoColorEmoji,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Android Emoji&quot;,EmojiSymbols;font-size:16px\">  <span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\">tau</span><span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,255)\"> </span>= exp( mu_p[2] + sigma[2] * <span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,0)\">tau_p</span> );</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif,Helvetica,EmojiFont,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,NotoColorEmoji,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Android Emoji&quot;,EmojiSymbols;font-size:16px\">}</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif,Helvetica,EmojiFont,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,NotoColorEmoji,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Android Emoji&quot;,EmojiSymbols;font-size:16px\">model {</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif,Helvetica,EmojiFont,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,NotoColorEmoji,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Android Emoji&quot;,EmojiSymbols;font-size:16px\">  # ra_prospect: Original model in Soko-Hessner et al 2009 PNAS</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif,Helvetica,EmojiFont,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,NotoColorEmoji,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Android Emoji&quot;,EmojiSymbols;font-size:16px\">  # hyper parameters</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif,Helvetica,EmojiFont,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,NotoColorEmoji,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Android Emoji&quot;,EmojiSymbols;font-size:16px\">  mu_p  ~ normal(0, 1.0); </div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif,Helvetica,EmojiFont,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,NotoColorEmoji,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Android Emoji&quot;,EmojiSymbols;font-size:16px\">  sigma ~ cauchy(0, 5.0);</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif,Helvetica,EmojiFont,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,NotoColorEmoji,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Android Emoji&quot;,EmojiSymbols;font-size:16px\">  </div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif,Helvetica,EmojiFont,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,NotoColorEmoji,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Android Emoji&quot;,EmojiSymbols;font-size:16px\">  # individual parameters w/ Matt trick</div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif,Helvetica,EmojiFont,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,NotoColorEmoji,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Android Emoji&quot;,EmojiSymbols;font-size:16px\">  <span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,0)\">rho_p</span> ~ normal(0, 1.0);   </div><div style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif,Helvetica,EmojiFont,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,NotoColorEmoji,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Android Emoji&quot;,EmojiSymbols;font-size:16px\">  <span style=\"background-color:rgb(255,255,0)\">tau_p</span> ~ normal(0, 1.0);</div><span style=\"font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif,Helvetica,EmojiFont,&quot;Apple Color Emoji&quot;,&quot;Segoe UI Emoji&quot;,NotoColorEmoji,&quot;Segoe UI Symbol&quot;,&quot;Android Emoji&quot;,EmojiSymbols;font-size:16px\"> ...</span> </code></pre>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\nHere, you can see that we are distributing the normal along rho_p and tau_p, and then transforming these into rho and tau. In this case, the adjustment is not necessary. \r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>I hope this helps! </div>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<div>Best,</div>\r\n<div>Nate<br>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<div><br>\r\n</div>\r\n<p></p>\r\n<p><br>\r\n</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<hr style=\"display:inline-block;width:98%\">\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\"><font face=\"Calibri, sans-serif\" style=\"font-size:11pt\" color=\"#000000\"><b>From:</b> <a rel=\"nofollow\">hbayesd...@googlegroups.com</a> &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">hbayesd...@googlegroups.com</a>&gt; on behalf of Joseph Galaro &lt;<a rel=\"nofollow\">jga...@gmail.com</a>&gt;<br>\r\n<b>Sent:</b> Friday, September 29, 2017 3:28:10 PM<br>\r\n<b>To:</b> hbayesdm-users<br>\r\n<b>Subject:</b> Jacobian adjustment term for logit-transformed estimation (ra_prospect, ra_noLA, ra_noRA)</font>\r\n<div> </div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div><div>\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\">Hi all,<br>\r\n<br>\r\nThank you to the creators for putting together this great package! It&#39;s been invaluable while learning to implement STAN models.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\nI&#39;m currently focused on extracting subjective preference parameters via STAN, as implemented in hBayesDM/ra_prospect. While researching the topic, I found this article (<a href=\"http://mc-stan.org/users/documentation/case-studies/mle-params.html\" rel=\"nofollow\" target=\"_blank\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://mc-stan.org/users/documentation/case-studies/mle-params.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1793243280364000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1SeRSYAQR37uXPUV42iiRY\">http://mc-stan.org/users/documentation/case-studies/mle-params.html</a>)\r\n describing the importance/impact of including the Jacobian term when calculating Bayesian estimates on logit transformed variables. I&#39;m still pretty new to STAN, but it appears the hBayesDM implementations of ra_prospect, ra_noLA, and ra_noRA don&#39;t include\r\n this term.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nI&#39;m trying to wrap my head around the validity of including the Jacobian adjustment, and would greatly appreciate if anyone could provide insight to why it is not included in the hBayesDM implementation.\r\n<br>\r\n<br>\r\nThank you for your help,<br>\r\nJoe</div>\r\n<p></p>\r\n-- <br>\r\nYou received this message because you are subscribed to the Google Groups &quot;hbayesdm-users&quot; group.<br>\r\nTo unsubscribe from this group and stop receiving emails from it, send an email to\r\n<a rel=\"nofollow\">hbayesdm-user...@googlegroups.com</a>.<br></div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div><div>\r\nTo post to this group, send email to <a rel=\"nofollow\">\r\nhbayes...@googlegroups.com</a>.</div></div></blockquote></div></div>"
